# GB native audio: lapis vendor_dlkm HDA codec modules (unsigned vendor modules, first taken from build 271's
# vendor_dlkm; byte-identical to lapis 276's copies, readiness C-7). Their modversion CRCs are checked against each
# kernel's vmlinux.symvers when it is built (k15: K15.md K-06, 0 mismatches) and their symbols are closed in
# this order. gbinit insmods them before Android init, so they are resident when ueventd autoloads
# snd-sof-pci-intel-icl and SOF probes the codecs. Without them SOF drops the ALC274 (GKI has no request_module) and
# there is no analog audio. If the booted slot's vendor_dlkm comes from another lapis build and its SOF modules
# reject these, gb_audio.sh unloads them and loads the vendor_dlkm copies instead (refresh with src/refresh_modules.sh).
# Append these lines to inject/native/modules/modules.load after i915.ko. The order within this block matters.
snd-hda-core.ko
snd-hda-codec.ko
snd-hda-codec-generic.ko
snd-hda-codec-realtek-lib.ko
snd-hda-scodec-component.ko
snd-hda-codec-alc269.ko
snd-hda-codec-hdmi.ko
snd-hda-codec-intelhdmi.ko
